nt":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# 🎯 Target Encoding\n\nTarget Encoding replaces categorical values with the average target value.\n\nOut-of-Fold Target Encoding is used to prevent data leakage during training.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"#OOF target encoding function\n\ndef add_oof_target_encoding(train_df, test_df, y_log, cols, n_splits=5, random_state=42):\n    train_df = train_df.copy()\n    test_df = test_df.copy()\n\n    kf = KFold(n_splits=n_splits, shuffle=True, random_state=random_state)\n    global_mean = y_log.mean()\n\n    for col in cols:\n        print(f\"OOF target encoding -> {col}\")\n\n        tr_col = train_df[col].astype(str).fillna(\"MISSING\")\n        te_col = test_df[col].astype(str).fillna(\"MISSING\")\n\n        oof_mean = np.zeros(len(train_df))\n        oof_median = np.zeros(len(train_df))\n        oof_std = np.zeros(len(train_df))\n\n        for tr_idx, val_idx in kf.split(train_df):\n            x_tr = tr_col.iloc[tr_idx]\n            x_val = tr_col.iloc[val_idx]\n            y_tr = y_log.iloc[tr_idx]\n\n            stats_df = pd.DataFrame({\n                col: x_tr.values,\n                \"target\": y_tr.values\n            })\n\n            agg = stats_df.groupby(col)[\"target\"].agg([\"mean\", \"median\", \"std\"])\n\n            mean_map = agg[\"mean\"].to_dict()\n            median_map = agg[\"median\"].to_dict()\n            std_map = agg[\"std\"].to_dict()\n\n            oof_mean[val_idx] = x_val.map(mean_map).fillna(global_mean).values\n            oof_median[val_idx] = x_val.map(median_map).fillna(global_mean).values\n            oof_std[val_idx] = x_val.map(std_map).fillna(0).values\n\n        full_stats = pd.DataFrame({\n            col: tr_col.values,\n            \"target\": y_log.values\n        }).groupby(col)[\"target\"].agg([\"mean\", \"median\", \"std\"])\n\n        train_df[col + \"_te_mean\"] = oof_mean\n        train_df[col + \"_te_median\"] = oof_median\n        train_df[col + \"_te_std\"] = oof_std\n\n        test_df[col + \"_te_mean\"] = te_col.map(full_stats[\"mean\"]).fillna(global_mean).values\n        test_df[col + \"_te_median\"] = te_col.map(full_stats[\"median\"]).fillna(global_mean).values\n        test_df[col + \"_te_std\"] = te_col.map(full_stats[\"std\"]).fillna(0).values\n\n    return train_df, test_df","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-07-21T07:42:56.609788Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-07-21T07:42:56.610221Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-07-21T07:42:56.622129Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-07-21T07:42:56.610179Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-07-21T07:42:56.620931Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# ✅ Apply Target Encoding\n\nNow we apply target encoding to important categorical columns.\n\nThese new features often improve model performance.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"\n#apply OOF target encoding\n\nte_candidates = []\n\nfor c in [\n    asset_col, product_col, vendor_col, region_col,\n    baseclass_col, subclass_col, inv_cat_col, func_class_col\n]:\n    if c is not None and c in train_df.columns:\n        te_candidates.append(c)\n\ncross_cols_created = [c for c in train_df.columns if \"__\" in c and train_df[c].dtype == \"object\"]\nte_candidates += cross_cols_created[:10]\n\nte_candidates = list(dict.fromkeys(te_candidates))\n\nprint(\"target encoding columns:\")\nprint(te_candidates)\n\ntrain_df, test_df = add_oof_target_encoding(\n    train_df=train_df,\n    test_df=test_df,\n    y_log=y,\n    cols=te_candidates,\n    n_splits=N_SPLITS,\n    random_state=RANDOM_STATE\n)\n\nprint(\"OOF target encoding completed\")\nprint(train_df.shape, test_df.shape)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-07-21T07:42:56.624672Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-07-21T07:42:56.62504Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-07-21T07:43:06.794467Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-07-21T07:42:56.625Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-07-21T07:43:06.793495Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# 📈 Group-based Statistical Features\n\nAggregated statistics such as mean, median and count are computed for important groups.\n\nThese features capture historical behaviour of different equipment categories.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"#group aggregation features\n\ndef add_group_stats(train_df, test_df, group_cols, num_cols_for_stats):\n    train_df = train_df.copy()\n    test_df = test_df.copy()\n\n    for gcol in group_cols:\n        if gcol is None or gcol not in train_df.columns:\n            continue\n\n        for ncol in num_cols_for_stats:\n            if ncol not in train_df.columns:\n                continue\n\n            full = pd.concat([train_df[[gcol, ncol]], test_df[[gcol, ncol]]], axis=0)\n\n            agg = full.groupby(gcol)[ncol].agg([\"mean\", \"median\", \"std\", \"min\", \"max\"])\n\n            for stat in [\"mean\", \"median\", \"std\", \"min\", \"max\"]:\n                train_df[f\"{gcol}_{ncol}_{stat}\"] = train_df[gcol].map(agg[stat])\n                test_df[f\"{gcol}_{ncol}_{stat}\"] = test_df[gcol].map(agg[stat])\n\n        full_count = pd.concat([train_df[gcol], test_df[gcol]], axis=0).value_counts(dropna=False)\n        train_df[gcol + \"_count_all\"] = train_df[gcol].map(full_count).astype(float)\n        test_df[gcol + \"_count_all\"] = test_df[gcol].map(full_count).astype(float)\n\n    return train_df, test_df\n\nnumeric_candidates = []\nfor c in train_df.columns:\n    if c == ID_COL:\n        continue\n    if train_df[c].dtype != \"object\":\n        numeric_candidates.append(c)\n\npriority_num_cols = []\nfor c in numeric_candidates:\n    lc = c.lower()\n    if any(k in lc for k in [\"year\", \"hour\", \"meter\", \"scale\", \"age\", \"freq\", \"te_mean\", \"te_median\"]):\n        priority_num_cols.append(c)\n\npriority_num_cols = list(dict.fromkeys(priority_num_cols))[:25]\n\ngroup_cols = [asset_col, product_col, vendor_col, region_col, baseclass_col, subclass_col]\n\nprint(\"group cols:\", group_cols)\nprint(\"numeric stats cols:\", priority_num_cols[:20])\n\ntrain_df, test_df = add_group_stats(train_df, test_df, group_cols, priority_num_cols)\n\nprint(\"group stats done\")\nprint(train_df.shape, test_df.shape)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-07-21T07:43:06.795585Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-07-21T07:43:06.796056Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-07-21T07:43:19.183778Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-07-21T07:43:06.796023Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-07-21T07:43:19.182879Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# 🧩 Final Feature Matrix\n\nAll engineered features are combined into the final feature matrix.\n\nThe same preprocessing steps are applied consistently to both training and test datasets.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"#final matrix prepare\n\nFEATURES = [c for c in train_df.columns if c != ID_COL]\n\nX = train_df[FEATURES].copy()\nX_test = test_df[FEATURES].copy()\n\nprint(\"feature count before encoding:\", len(FEATURES))\n\ncat_cols_final = X.select_dtypes(include=[\"object\"]).columns.tolist()\nprint(\"object columns to label encode:\", len(cat_cols_final))\n\nfor col in cat_cols_final:\n    le = LabelEncoder()\n\n    full_values = pd.concat([X[col], X_test[col]], axis=0).astype(str).fillna(\"MISSING\")\n    le.fit(full_values)\n\n    X[col] = le.transform(X[col].astype(str).fillna(\"MISSING\"))\n    X_test[col] = le.transform(X_test[col].astype(str).fillna(\"MISSING\"))\n\nfor col in X.columns:\n    if X[col].dtype == \"int64\":\n        X[col] = X[col].astype(np.int32)\n        X_test[col] = X_test[col].astype(np.int32)\n    elif X[col].dtype == \"float64\":\n        X[col] = X[col].astype(np.float32)\n        X_test[col] = X_test[col].astype(np.float32)\n\nfor col in X.columns:\n    if X[col].dtype in [np.float32, np.float64, np.int32, np.int64]:\n        train_med = X[col].median()\n        X[col] = X[col].fillna(train_med)\n        X_test[col] = X_test[col].fillna(train_med)\n\nprint(\"Final X shape     :\", X.shape)\nprint(\"Final X_test shape:\", X_test.shape)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-07-21T07:43:19.185187Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-07-21T07:43:19.185539Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-07-21T07:43:37.575592Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-07-21T07:43:19.185501Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-07-21T07:43:37.574265Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# 🔄 Reusable Preprocessing Pipeline\n\nTo improve reproducibility and reduce redundant code, preprocessing is organized using a reusable `ColumnTransformer` and `Pipeline`.\n\nThe preprocessing workflow ensures:\n\n- A consistent transformation is applied during training and inference.\n- Redundant preprocessing code is avoided.\n- The workflow is easier to reproduce and maintain.\n- The same preprocessing logic can be reused for unseen test data.\n\n**Note:** In this notebook, feature engineering and encoding have already been completed before this demonstration. Therefore, the `ColumnTransformer` is configured with `passthrough` to illustrate how preprocessing can be organized inside a reusable pipeline without modifying the final feature matrix used for model training.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Demonstration of ColumnTransformer\npreprocessor = ColumnTransformer(\n    transformers=[\n        (\"all_features\", \"passthrough\", X.columns.tolist())\n    ]\n)\n\ndemo_pipeline = Pipeline([\n    (\"preprocessor\", preprocessor)\n])\n\nX_demo = demo_pipeline.fit_transform(X)\n\nprint(\"Original Shape :\", X.shape)\nprint(\"After ColumnTransformer :\", X_demo.shape)\n\nassert X.shape == X_demo.shape\nprint(\"ColumnTransformer demonstration completed.\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-07-21T07:43:37.577243Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-07-21T07:43:37.57768Z",